# Project Structure and Organization

## Objective
Maintain a clean, scalable, and logical project structure that supports the Downlodr application's architecture and enables team collaboration.

## Context
- Electron desktop application with React frontend
- TypeScript for type safety and better development experience
- Component-based architecture with clear separation of concerns
- Plugin system requiring modular organization
- Cross-platform builds with Electron Forge

## Rules

### Root Directory Organization

#### Core Configuration Files
- **Root level**: Keep configuration files at project root
  ```
  ✅ package.json, tsconfig.json, tailwind.config.js
  ✅ forge.config.ts, vite.*.config.ts
  ✅ .eslintrc.json, .prettierrc
  ❌ config/package.json, src/tsconfig.json
  ```

#### Source Code Structure
- **src/**: All source code must be in src directory
- **Clear separation**: Separate main process, renderer, and preload scripts
  ```
  ✅ src/main.ts (Electron main process)
  ✅ src/renderer.tsx (React app entry)
  ✅ src/preload.ts (Electron preload script)
  ❌ main.ts, renderer.tsx (in root)
  ```

### Component Organization

#### Directory Hierarchy
- **Components/**: Primary UI components
  - **Main/**: Core application components (layout, navigation)
  - **SubComponents/**: Reusable and utility components
    - **custom/**: Project-specific components
    - **shadcn/**: Third-party UI library components
  ```
  ✅ Components/Main/Modal/SettingsModal.tsx
  ✅ Components/SubComponents/custom/DownloadButton.tsx
  ✅ Components/SubComponents/shadcn/components/ui/button.tsx
  ❌ Components/SettingsModal.tsx
  ❌ UI/Button.tsx
  ```

#### Component File Structure
- **Single component per file**: One main export per component file
- **Co-location**: Related types and utilities near component usage
- **Index files**: Use for clean imports when beneficial
  ```typescript
  ✅ // DownloadButton.tsx
  interface DownloadButtonProps {}
  export const DownloadButton: React.FC<DownloadButtonProps> = () => {};
  
  ✅ // Icons/index.tsx
  export { Download } from './Download';
  export { Settings } from './Settings';
  ```

### Feature-Based Organization

#### Pages and Layouts
- **Pages/**: Top-level page components
- **Layout/**: Layout wrapper components
- **SubPages/**: Nested or specialized page components
  ```
  ✅ Pages/History.tsx
  ✅ Pages/SubPages/CategoryPage.tsx
  ✅ Layout/MainLayout.tsx
  ❌ Components/Pages/History.tsx
  ❌ Pages/Layout/MainLayout.tsx
  ```

#### Domain-Specific Modules
- **Store/**: State management (Zustand stores)
- **plugins/**: Plugin system implementation
- **schema/**: Type definitions and schemas
- **DataFunctions/**: Business logic and data processing
  ```
  ✅ Store/downloadStore.tsx
  ✅ plugins/types.ts, plugins/pluginAPI.ts
  ✅ schema/download.ts, schema/metadata.ts
  ✅ DataFunctions/updateChecker.ts
  ```

### Asset Management

#### Static Assets
- **Assets/**: All static assets in organized subdirectories
- **Logical grouping**: Group by type and usage
  ```
  ✅ Assets/AppLogo/256x256.ico
  ✅ Assets/Icons/Download.tsx
  ✅ Assets/Images/FormatConverter.jpg
  ❌ images/logo.ico
  ❌ Assets/download-icon.tsx
  ```

#### Asset Naming
- **Descriptive names**: Clear indication of content and usage
- **Size specifications**: Include dimensions for icons/images where relevant
- **Platform variants**: Separate platform-specific assets
  ```
  ✅ systemTray/logo/systemIcon.png
  ✅ AppLogo/256x256.ico
  ❌ icon.png, logo.ico
  ```

### Plugin System Structure

#### Plugin Organization
- **plugins/**: All plugin-related code
- **Separation of concerns**: Components, hooks, types, and utilities
  ```
  ✅ plugins/types.ts
  ✅ plugins/components/PluginModalManager.tsx
  ✅ plugins/Hooks/usePluginState.ts
  ✅ plugins/security.ts
  ❌ Components/PluginComponents/
  ❌ Hooks/PluginHooks/
  ```

#### Plugin Components
- **Manager pattern**: Centralized management components
- **Extension pattern**: Components that extend functionality
  ```
  ✅ PluginModalManager.tsx
  ✅ PluginSidePanelExtension.tsx
  ✅ FormatSelectorManager.tsx
  ❌ PluginModal.tsx
  ❌ SidePanel.tsx
  ```

### Utility and Helper Organization

#### Utility Functions
- **Utils/**: Generic utility functions
- **DataFunctions/**: Business logic and data processing
- **Descriptive naming**: Clear indication of functionality
  ```
  ✅ Utils/stringHelpers.ts
  ✅ Utils/iconHelpers.tsx
  ✅ DataFunctions/GetDownloadMetaData.ts
  ✅ DataFunctions/ErrorCodeHelper.ts
  ❌ helpers.ts, utils.ts
  ```

#### Type Definitions
- **schema/**: Centralized type definitions and schemas
- **global.d.ts**: Global type augmentations
- **Co-located types**: Component-specific types near components
  ```
  ✅ schema/download.ts, schema/metadata.ts
  ✅ global.d.ts (window API extensions)
  ✅ plugins/types.ts (plugin-specific types)
  ```

### Configuration and Build

#### Build Configuration
- **Separate configs**: Different Vite configs for different targets
- **Environment-specific**: Development vs production configurations
  ```
  ✅ vite.main.config.ts (main process)
  ✅ vite.renderer.config.ts (renderer process)
  ✅ vite.preload.config.ts (preload script)
  ❌ vite.config.ts (single config)
  ```

#### Documentation
- **docs/**: Comprehensive documentation in separate directory
- **Inline documentation**: JSDoc for functions and components
  ```
  ✅ docs/architecture.md
  ✅ docs/PLUGIN_DEVELOPMENT.MD
  ✅ README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md (root level)
  ```

### Import Path Management

#### Path Aliases
- **@/ alias**: Use for src directory references
- **Relative imports**: Only for nearby files (same directory or parent)
- **Absolute imports**: For cross-feature dependencies
  ```typescript
  ✅ import { useMainStore } from '@/Store/mainStore';
  ✅ import { Button } from '@/Components/SubComponents/shadcn/components/ui/button';
  ✅ import './LocalStyles.css'; // Same directory
  ❌ import { useMainStore } from '../../../Store/mainStore';
  ```

#### Import Organization
- **Logical grouping**: External libraries, internal modules, relative imports
- **Alphabetical within groups**: Consistent ordering within import groups
  ```typescript
  ✅
  // External libraries
  import React from 'react';
  import { create } from 'zustand';
  
  // Internal modules
  import { useMainStore } from '@/Store/mainStore';
  import { DownloadButton } from '@/Components/SubComponents/custom/DownloadButton';
  
  // Relative imports
  import './Component.css';
  ```

## Exceptions
- **Third-party components**: May follow library-specific organization
- **Legacy migrations**: Gradual restructuring acceptable with clear plan
- **Generated files**: Auto-generated files may have different structure
- **Platform-specific code**: May require different organization patterns

## Enforcement
- Path alias configuration in tsconfig.json and Vite config
- ESLint import rules for consistent import patterns
- Code review checklist for structural consistency
- Documentation updates when structure changes

